    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a burrito\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for taqueria al pastor built on cheap thigh instead of a trompo. The achiote brick and a can of pineapple do most of the flavor for almost nothing.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "Achiote paste comes in a cheap little brick that lasts for months and gives al pastor its brick red color and earthy flavor. One block seasons many batches.",
                       "Chicken thigh is the right cut here and it is cheaper than breast. Buy the family pack and freeze what this batch does not use.",
                       "A can of pineapple chunks is cheaper and more consistent than a fresh pineapple, and you want the juice for the marinade too, so nothing goes to waste.",
                       "Dried ancho chiles cost little in the bagged section of the Mexican aisle. Toast and grind a couple and you have the real thing instead of a dusty jar of chili powder."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Toast the dried ancho chiles in a dry pan for a minute, then blend them with the garlic, chipotle in adobo, orange juice, brown sugar, achiote paste, ground cumin and salt into a smooth marinade.",
                    "Coat the chicken thighs in the marinade and let them sit at least 30 minutes.",
                    "Cook the rice until tender and set it aside.",
                    "Sear or grill the marinated thighs until charred at the edges and cooked through, then chop them.",
                    "Char the pineapple chunks and the sliced onion in a hot dry pan until they take on color.",
                    "Weigh the rice, chicken, pineapple and onion together, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14. Lay that much down each tortilla, scatter on chopped cilantro, fold in the sides and roll.",
                    "Wrap each burrito and portion into 14 containers."
                ],
    "portion_html":  "Weigh the filling, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14 so every burrito gets the same char and sweetness. Each burrito carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e. Reheat wrapped, and the pineapple keeps it juicy.",
